WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.515
Word Search Studio began as a C plus plus
console game.

00:00:03.515 --> 00:00:07.225
The browser edition keeps its fifteen-by-
fifteen board and difficulty rules, while

00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:11.410
adding accessible controls, automatic resume,
and an explanation of the search.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.430
A seeded random sequence makes the same
puzzle reproducible for the

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.885
same rules and generator version. Daily
puzzles derive that seed from

00:00:17.885 --> 00:00:20.195
a shared U T C date, rather than storing a
new

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:22.050
random board for every visitor.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.130
The generator tries bounded placements for
each target. Matching letters may

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.920
overlap. Only successfully placed words enter
the target list. Random letters

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.805
fill the empty cells afterwards, so listed
targets remain achievable.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:39.565
Easy allows horizontal lines. Intermediate
adds vertical lines, and hard adds

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:44.025
diagonals. The selected cells must form a
straight permitted path. Forward

00:00:44.025 --> 00:00:46.995
and reverse selections resolve to the same
canonical target.

00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:50.685
A newly found word earns ten points.
Selecting it again earns

00:00:50.685 --> 00:00:54.940
nothing and costs no life. Classic mode
penalises wrong attempts, while

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.975
relaxed mode lets a student explore without
that penalty.

00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:01.345
The algorithm view highlights candidate
starts and directions until it finds

00:01:01.345 --> 00:01:06.835
a match. Tests check generation, permitted
paths, reverse selection, and
reproducibility.

00:01:06.835 --> 00:01:09.490
Personal records stay in the browser; they
are not a verified

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:10.875
global leaderboard.
